     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Sertraline 1000 mg/day is far beyond any labeled or guideline-supported dose, and I don't know of any evidence supporting it. A single dose that size could cause serious harm.\n\nIf the dose really is intentional, these steps would get it through safely:\n- **Pharmacy review:** ask the clinical pharmacist to review and verify the dose.\n- **Direct confirmation:** have the specialist or attending enter the order themselves or co-sign it. They can document their rationale and a monitoring plan, such as ECG/QTc, serotonin syndrome checks, and sodium.\n- **Alternatives:** if standard dosing failed, the specialist may want to consider other options. Examples are switching agents, augmentation, or doses up to 200 mg/day.\n\nI can enter sertraline at a dose within the recommended range, up to 200 mg once daily, if you'd like. I can also add a note to an order that asks for pharmacy review."
      }
     ],
